class.description:
Obtained from [method NetwDatabase.table]. Every verb answers a [NetwPromise], and the value arrives through [method NetwPromise.wait], because the database may be reading from a disk or a socket and native code cannot suspend on the caller's behalf.
[codeblock]
# Read a record and one of its columns:
var record: NetwRecord = await db.table(&"players").fetch(username).wait()
if record:
    var score := record.get_value(&"score", 0)

# Write it back, and remove it:
var err: Error = await db.table(&"players").put(username, record).wait()
await db.table(&"players").erase(username).wait()

# Read the whole table:
for row in await db.table(&"players").fetch_all().wait():
    print(row.get_value(&"score"))
[/codeblock]
The handle is minted per call and holds no cache, so keeping one is the same as asking for it again. What it hands back is a [DictionaryRecord] unless [method NetwDatabase.declare_table] registered a [NetwRecord] subclass for the table, in which case every read answers that type.
[codeblock]
db.declare_table(&"rocks", [&"health", &"position"], RockRecord)
var rock: RockRecord = await db.table(&"rocks").fetch(&"rock_1").wait()
[/codeblock]

method.description:
Reads every record matching [param filter] and settles with them as an [Array] of [NetwRecord]. An empty [param filter] answers the whole table, and a table with nothing in it answers an empty array rather than failing.
[codeblock]
var online := await db.table(&"players").fetch_all(
        {&"online": true},
).wait()
[/codeblock]
